    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Add an explicit 'Requires: soapy-sdr' to the module subpackage.

Requested by dimstar reviewing the soapy-plutosdr submission (sr#1374694,
since superseded to sr#1374739):
&quot;Shouldn't that require soapy-sdr? The module on its own seems quite useless&quot;.
Applied here to the whole SoapySDR plugin set rather than to that one package.

To be precise about what this does and does not do: libSoapySDR is what dlopens
the module, and that is already covered by the automatic soname dependency on
libSoapySDR.so.0.8-3 - it is not what was missing. What the module did not pull
in is the soapy-sdr package proper, which ships SoapySDRUtil, the tool used to
enumerate and probe devices. That is the gap this closes.

Note on precedent: no SoapySDR plugin currently released in Factory carries
this dependency (checked soapy-rtlsdr, soapy-hackrf, soapy-airspy, soapy-osmo,
soapy-uhd), so this is a deliberate tightening rather than an existing
convention. It is being applied across the plugin set, not to this package
alone.

Also in this request:

- License corrected from LGPL-2.1-only to LGPL-2.1-or-later. All four source
  files (bladeRF_Registration.cpp, bladeRF_Settings.cpp, bladeRF_Streaming.cpp,
  bladeRF_SoapySDR.hpp) carry the standard header granting &quot;version 2.1 of the
  License, or (at your option) any later version&quot;. The bare &quot;LGPL-2.1&quot; in
  upstream's debian/copyright is the old Debian shorthand, not a restriction.
- Declared the SoapySDR floor upstream actually checks for: CMakeLists.txt has
  find_package(SoapySDR &quot;0.4&quot; NO_MODULE), so pkgconfig(SoapySDR) &gt;= 0.4. No
  floor for libbladeRF - upstream's FindLibbladeRF.cmake probes it unversioned.
- spec-cleaner pass: bladeRF-devel -&gt; pkgconfig(libbladeRF), soapy-sdr-devel -&gt;
  pkgconfig(SoapySDR), %setup -&gt; %autosetup.

No version bump. 0.4.2 (2024-12-22) is still upstream's newest tag. master is
three commits ahead, but the entire diff against the tag is two lines - a
cmake_minimum_required bump and a one-line RX2/TX2 streaming fix - and
upstream's Changelog.txt has no pending-release section, so there is nothing
worth snapshotting.

Built locally on Tumbleweed/aarch64; rpmlint reports 0 errors, 0 warnings,
0 badness. The only change to the installed RPM is the License tag and the
added dependency.</comment>
    <requestid>1374755</requestid>
